~ start
The Guardian: It looks like a forest of stone... The air whistles without harmony here.
The Guardian: These monumental flutes are broken. They must be rebuilt.
=> END

~ indice_stele
The Guardian: "From the rumbling of the earth to the whistling of the summit."
The Guardian: That means from longest to shortest. Low pitch to High pitch.
=> END

~ lecon_inca
Incan Spirit: Stranger, listen to the lesson of the Andes.
Incan Spirit: A long tube holds the breath: it creates a Low sound.
Incan Spirit: A short tube releases the air quickly: it creates a High sound.
=> END

~ success
The Guardian: Listen! The air is flowing perfectly.
The Guardian: The melody is pure... the passage is open!
=> END